# nestjs-tronweb-example

Small, production-oriented NestJS module wrapping [TronWeb](https://github.com/tronprotocol/tronweb):

- Injectable `TronWeb` provider (`TronWebModule.forRoot` / `forRootAsync`)
- `TronService` helpers for TRC-20 `balanceOf` and `transfer`
- Typed `TronCallError` with kinds for invalid address/amount, contract revert, node/network, and configuration mistakes

This lives **outside** TronWeb core docs (per maintainer guidance on [tronweb#713](https://github.com/tronprotocol/tronweb/issues/713)) and complements the Shasta/script-focused work in [tronweb#714](https://github.com/tronprotocol/tronweb/pull/714).

## Install

```bash
npm install tronweb @nestjs/common @nestjs/core reflect-metadata rxjs
# then copy/use this module, or depend on this repo once published
```

## Quick start

```ts
import { Module } from '@nestjs/common';
import { TronWebModule, TronService } from './index'; // or package path

@Module({
  imports: [
    TronWebModule.forRootAsync({
      useFactory: () => ({
        fullHost: process.env.TRON_FULL_HOST || 'https://api.shasta.trongrid.io',
        headers: process.env.TRON_API_KEY
          ? { 'TRON-PRO-API-KEY': process.env.TRON_API_KEY }
          : undefined,
        privateKey: process.env.TRON_PRIVATE_KEY, // optional; required for transfer
        defaultTrc20Contract: process.env.TRC20_CONTRACT,
      }),
    }),
  ],
})
export class AppModule {}
```

Inject `TronService`:

```ts
constructor(private readonly tron: TronService) {}

async check(owner: string, contract: string) {
  return this.tron.getTrc20Balance(owner, contract);
}

async send(to: string, amountSmallestUnits: string, contract: string) {
  return this.tron.transferTrc20({ contractAddress: contract, to, amount: amountSmallestUnits });
}
```

## Error-handling notes

| Kind | When it surfaces | Suggested handling |
|------|------------------|--------------------|
| `invalid_address` | Bad base58 / hex address | Validate inputs before calling; return 400 |
| `invalid_amount` | Non-integer / negative amount | Amounts must be **smallest units** (respect decimals) |
| `contract_revert` | On-chain revert (e.g. insufficient balance) | Surface user-safe message; log raw cause |
| `node_or_network` | Timeout, 5xx, DNS, connection refused | Retry with backoff; switch endpoint if needed |
| `configuration` | Missing `fullHost`, private key, or default contract | Fail fast at boot / return 500 with clear ops message |

Never log private keys. Prefer TronGrid API keys via headers, and keep signing keys in a secrets manager / HSM for production.

Official contract interaction docs: https://tronweb.network/docu/docs/Interact%20with%20contract#read--write-typed-namespaces

## Run the demo context

```bash
cp .env.example .env
npm install
npx ts-node src/example/main.ts
```

